 #:seon.task{:name "test-messages-print-whole-worlds"
             :kind :function
             :intent "pr-str outside the floor printer copies whole values. clojure.test evaluates an is message even when the assertion passes, so (is ... (pr-str outcomes)) printed hosted agents (their cluster handle's roster atom holds every context's projection) and a candidate result with its SCI context: `seon.cluster.host-test/one-identity-is-homed-on-one-branch-decided-by-the-writer` and seon.test.accretion-test/a-gate-test-runs-with-its-authors-cluster-custody each died after 20 s with OutOfMemoryError in a StringWriter. Test messages and failure-path text print through bounded-text (or name the fields they assert); production sites that print arbitrary values: web.clj create-owner-response and context-action-response 422 bodies, db.clj value-type-error and pull-call messages, problems.clj ai-prose offending, cluster.clj mcp-plain."
             :must-read #{seon.render.value/bounded-text}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/landing/oom-array-opus-2026-09-27.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-lazy-seq-that-throws-shows-as-empty"
             :kind :function
             :intent "When realizing a lazy seq throws while the floor prints it, prepare's retry prints the same seq again; Clojure 1.12.5 leaves a LazySeq empty after its body throws, so the agent sees () beside the diagnostic, a wrong value. The diagnostic also names the renderer when the floor itself failed, and it is a ;; comment line, not data. Show the realized prefix and the failure as data (probed by fix-a-floor-opus, c32b272f9)."
             :must-read #{seon.render.value/prepare}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/red-triage-3-2026-09-27.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "an-uncut-string-node-carries-no-total"
             :kind :function
             :intent "The floor's tree gives collection nodes `:seon.render.data/total` always but string nodes only when cut, so a consumer cannot tell an uncut string page's end; mcp-get-value (999fb0450) now derives it from the page's shape. Give the uncut :string node its total at the producer, then delete that special case in seon.cluster/mcp-get-value. Tried through the REPL 2026-09-27 (repl-dogfood): the one-line change (the uncut node gets (+ (:base node 0) (:total node)), the absolute total a cut names) is proven on real selections and its regression is red on the base, but it cannot install: tree's contract [:=> [:cat :map :map] :map] fails the auto-check (nil for empty nodes) and the gate refuses every reaching file test; tighten the contract to a node map holding root id 0."
             :must-read #{seon.render.value/tree seon.cluster/mcp-get-value}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/red-triage-3-2026-09-27.md"
                         "docs/research/agent-platform/repl-dogfood-2026-09-27.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-count-prints-as-an-entity-reference"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Wrong value shown to agents: a JVM eval returning {`:seon.turn/agent` 61 ...} (query counts) printed each integer as [:db/ident `:seon.source/digest`] / [:db/ident :my.plan/current-step] — the floor treated small integers as entity ids and printed their referent's ident (observed via MCP eval_clj, 2026-09-27). A number is a number unless its schema says ref: reference printing applies only where the value's declared schema is `:seon.db/ref` (or a datom's ref attribute), never by guessing from the value. Still red on default (2026-10-12, JVM mode): `{:seon.turn/agent 61 :seon.source/digest 7}` and `{:seon.turn/agent 61 :seon.agent/id \"a\"}` print 61 as `[:db/ident :seon.agent/failure]`. Cause: `seon.render.value/prepare` marks a map `:entity?` when it holds any installed identity attribute, not only `:db/id`, and `seon.render.value/reference-value` then resolves an integer under a ref attribute; `{:seon.turn/agent 61 :x 3}` prints correctly. Fix at `prepare`/`reference-value`: an integer under a ref attribute is an entity id only in a map that carries `:db/id` (a pull or entity row); a map keyed by identity attributes is data. Done when the implementer adds these two maps as rows to `seon.render.value-test/a-reference-prints-as-its-referent-s-identity` (assert `:seon.render.value/text` equals `{:seon.turn/agent 61, :seon.agent/id \"a\"}` order as printed) and the row with `:db/id 7` stays green."
             :must-read #{seon.render.value/prepare seon.render.value/reference-value}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/repl-session-entity-design-2026-09-27.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-short-identifier-string-is-cut-at-its-first-chunk"
             :kind :function
             :intent "An MCP JVM eval returning 9 contract findings (maps of :row :col :level :type :filename :message) showed every :filename as \"/Users/sean/src/\"…+23 with a subs dig form (default 2026-09-27): breadth before depth spread the budget so each string stayed at its 16-character first chunk, and the path, the one member that identifies the finding, was unreadable while :type and :level printed whole. Rule 5 grows strings by doubling chunks but charges a path like prose. Done when a string that fits the remaining budget at its level prints whole before sibling collections expand (or short strings count as scalars), with a regression over a vector of such finding maps."
             :must-read #{seon.render.value/prepare}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-cut-operation-in-render-data-is-not-runnable"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Render data's cuts name no handle, so an offered operation the budget reaches last prints as (`seon.render.walk/related` …1): its request map is cut and the form cannot be run (`seon.test/run`'s related data, 2026-09-28). An operation is a whole form or absent. Done when a `:seon.render/operations` form inside render data prints whole or is dropped whole, with a regression."
             :must-read #{seon.render.value/select-nodes seon.render.walk/related}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/task-census/evidence/related_data--proof.clj"}}

 #:seon.task{:name "short-strings-in-pairs-are-cut"
            :kind :function
            :intent "A 32-row vector of [string long] pairs (a profile summary, strings of 40-60 characters) printed each string cut at 32 characters with a dig form per row, and a java.util.HashMap$Node printed as #object: the budget went to cut markers instead of the text. Done when a small tuple's string prints whole under the budget and a Map.Entry prints as its pair."
            :must-read #{seon.render.value/prepare}
            :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/task-census/evidence/mcp-dogfood--probe.clj"}}
