             :kind :function
             :intent "Render dedup: seon.print.value/bounded-text and throwable-text are the survivors (6618eda17); `seon.render.value/bounded-text` and its floor delegates remain until config.clj, test/runner.clj, cluster/wake.clj and render/var.clj convert, plus three test-fixture subjects and task/doc refs. Also the D1 (context owner out of web), D3, D4, D5 and D8 duplicates of the render-dedup series. Done when `seon.render.value/bounded-text` is deleted and every caller converted in the same commit, lint clean."
             :must-read #{seon.print.value/bounded-text seon.render.value/bounded-text seon.repl/entity-emission}}
 #:seon.task{:name "cuts-cost-more-than-they-hide-across-siblings",
            :kind :function,
            :intent
            "Breadth before depth spends the budget on one cut per member: a vector of 50 eleven-line sources at 1,500 tokens shows the first whole, then 31 strings each cut at 64 characters with a 45-character subs form, and a health report shows four collapsed cache-kind maps as {…8 (get-in result/e… [`:seon.health/cache` `:seon.cache/kinds` :seon.cluster/file-derivation-key])}, each cut longer than the eight numbers it hides. Done when a level whose members would each be cut admits fewer members whole and folds the rest into the tail count, decided by cost, with a regression on these two shapes.",
